<p class="text-highlight">Business investment growth has been relatively robust but uncertainty is projected to weigh a little on investment decisions in the near term.</p>
<p>Business investment has been relatively robust, growing by 4.3% over 2025. That strength was largely concentrated in non-residual buildings and structures assets, and in utilities industries. Growth in other subcomponents of business investment was weaker.</p>
<p>Business investment is expected to fall by 0.6% in 2026 H1 relative to 2025 H2, down from around 1% growth anticipated in the February Report. That is consistent with a small impact from higher uncertainty following the onset of conflict in the Middle East. Agency intelligence suggests that a protracted conflict is likely to dent investment intentions. The share of firms reporting that overall uncertainty was high or very high has risen in the last few months (Chart 1.11), but it remains lower than the 2022 peak. </p>
