<p>All illustrative policy paths assume that monetary policy makers know which scenario is going to unfold. In reality, there is uncertainty so, as well as considering what would be the appropriate policy response for different scenarios, policymakers can also assess whether and how to set policy robustly across a range of possible scenarios. Over time, the MPC can monitor the economic outlook to update its view of the risks around it and the appropriate policy strategy.</p>
